n\nNext game leads to (2,4) [absorbing] or (0,4). So E(1,3) = 1 + (2/3)*0 + (1/3)E(0,4)\n\n6. (-1,3):\n\nNext game leads to (0,4) or (-2,4) [absorbing]. So E(-1,3) = 1 + (2/3)E(0,4) + (1/3)*0\n\n7. (0,4):\n\nNext game leads to (1,5) or (-1,5). So E(0,4) = 1 + (2/3)E(1,5) + (1/3)E(-1,5)\n\n8. (1,5):\n\nNext game leads to (2,6) [absorbing] or (0,6) [absorbing]. So E(1,5) = 1 + (2/3)*0 + (1/3)*0 = 1\n\nSimilarly, 9. (-1,5):\n\nNext game leads to (0,6) [absorbing] or (-2,6) [absorbing]. So E(-1,5) = 1 + (2/3)*0 + (1/3)*0 = 1\n\nSo, the equations we have are:\n\n1. E(0,0) = 1 + (2/3)E(1,1) + (1/3)E(-1,1)\n\n2. E(1,1) = 1 + (1/3)E(0,2)\n\n3. E(-1,1) = 1 + (2/3)E(0,2)\n\n4. E(0,2) = 1 + (2/3)E(1,3) + (1/3)E(-1,3)\n\n5. E(1,3) = 1 + (1/3)E(0,4)\n\n6. E(-1,3) = 1 + (2/3)E(0,4)\n\n7. E(0,4) = 1 + (2/3)E(1,5) + (1/3)E(-1,5)\n\n8. E(1,5) = 1\n\n9. E(-1,5) = 1\n\nNow, we can solve these equations step by step starting from the bottom (the states with higher n first).\n\nFirst, equations 8 and 9 give E(1,5) = E(-1,5) = 1.\n\nPlugging into equation 7:\n\nE(0,4) = 1 + (2/3)(1) + (1/3)(1) = 1 + (2/3 + 1/3) = 1 + 1 = 2\n\nSo E(0,4) = 2.\n\nNow, equations 5 and 6:\n\nE(1,3) = 1 + (1/3)E(0,4) = 1 + (1/3)(2) = 1 + 2/3 = 5/3 \u2248 1.6667\n\nE(-1,3) = 1 + (2/3)E(0,4) = 1 + (2/3)(2) = 1 + 4/3 = 7/3 \u2248 2.3333\n\nThen, equation 4:\n\nE(0,2) = 1 + (2/3)E(1,3) + (1/3)E(-1,3) = 1 + (2/3)(5/3) + (1/3)(7/3)\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n(2/3)(5/3) = 10/9\n\n(1/3)(7/3) = 7/9\n\nSo total: 1 + 10/9 + 7/9 = 1 + 17/9 = (9/9 + 17/9) = 26/9 \u2248 2.8889\n\nSo E(0,2) = 26/9.\n\nNext, equations 2 and 3:\n\nE(1,1) = 1 + (1/3)E(0,2) = 1 + (1/3)(26/9) = 1 + 26/27 = 53/27 \u2248 1.9630\n\nE(-1,1) = 1 + (2/3)E(0,2) = 1 + (2/3)(26/9) = 1 + 52/27 = (27/27 + 52/27) = 79/27 \u2248 2.9259\n\nFinally, equation 1:\n\nE(0,0) = 1 + (2/3)E(1,1) + (1/3)E(-1,1) = 1 + (2/3)(53/27) + (1/3)(79/27)\n\nCompute each term:\n\n(2/3)(53/27) = (106)/81\n\n(1/3)(79/27) = 79/81\n\nAdding them up: 106/81 + 79/81 = 185/81\n\nThen E(