mes:\n     \\[\n     P(\\xi = 4) = P(\\text{\u7532\u8d623\u5c40\uff0c\u5176\u4e2d\u4e59\u8d621\u5c40}) + P(\\text{\u4e59\u8d623\u5c40\uff0c\u5176\u4e2d\u7532\u8d621\u5c40})\n     \\]\n     - There are various ways this could occur, where \u7532 wins 3 out of 4 games or \u4e59 wins 3 out of 4 games:\n     \\[\n     P(\\xi = 4) = 2 \\left[ \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^3 \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^3 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\right]\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 2 \\left[ \\frac{8}{81} + \\frac{2}{81} \\right] = 2 \\left[ \\frac{10}{81} \\right] = \\frac{20}{81}\n     \\]\n     \n   - The probability that the competition stops after exactly \\(6\\) games:\n     \\[\n     P(\\xi = 6) = 1 - P(\\xi = 2) - P(\\xi = 4)\n     \\]\n     Substitute values:\n     \\[\n     P(\\xi = 6) = 1 - \\frac{5}{9} - \\frac{20}{81}\n     \\]\n     Convert terms to a common denominator:\n     \\[\n     P(\\xi = 6) = \\frac{81}{81} - \\frac{45}{81} - \\frac{20}{81} = \\frac{81 - 45 - 20}{81} = \\frac{16}{81}\n     \\]\n \n3. **Expectation Calculation**:\n   To find the expected value \\( E(\\xi) \\):\n   \\[\n   E(\\xi) = 2 \\times P(\\xi = 2) + 4 \\times P(\\xi = 4) + 6 \\times P(\\xi = 6)\n   \\]\n   Substitute probabilities:\n   \\[\n   E(\\xi) = 2 \\times \\frac{5}{9} + 4 \\times \\frac{20}{81} + 6 \\times \\frac{16}{81}\n   \\]\n   Simplify each term:\n   \\[\n   = \\frac{2 \\times 5}{9} + \\frac{4 \\times 20}{81} + \\frac{6 \\times 16}{81}\n   = \\frac{10}{9} + \\frac{80}{81} + \\frac{96}{81}\n   \\]\n   Convert \\(\\frac{10}{9}\\) to a common denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{10}{9} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{9 \\times 9} = \\frac{90}{81}\n   \\]\n   Combine the fractions:\n   \\[\n   E(\\xi) = \\frac{90}{81} + \\frac{80}{81} + \\frac{96}{81} = \\frac{90 + 80 + 96}{81} = \\frac{266}{81}\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{266}{81}}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "A king has eight