t{Area}(\\triangle CBD) = \\frac{1}{2} S \\).\n\n2. Let \\( \\frac{BO}{BD} = x \\).\n\n3. We calculate the area of \\( \\triangle BMN \\):\n   - This area is given by the product of the fractions of the segments divided by \\( M \\) and \\( N \\) from \\( A \\) and \\( C \\) respectively, multiplied by the total area \\( S \\):\n     \\[\n     S_{\\triangle BMN} = \\frac{BM}{AB} \\cdot \\frac{BN}{BC} \\cdot S = \\frac{1}{m+1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{n+1} \\cdot S\n     \\]\n\n4. We decompose the area \\( S_{\\triangle BMN} \\) using \\( O \\) as follows:\n   \\[\n   S_{\\triangle BMN} = S_{\\triangle BMO} + S_{\\triangle BNO}\n   \\]\n\n5. Considering \\( S_{\\triangle BMO} \\) and \\( S_{\\triangle BNO} \\):\n   - The area \\( S_{\\triangle BMO} \\) is given as:\n     \\[\n     S_{\\triangle BMO} = \\frac{1}{m+1} \\cdot x \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} S\n     \\]\n   - Similarly, the area \\( S_{\\triangle BNO} \\) is:\n     \\[\n     S_{\\triangle BNO} = \\frac{1}{n+1} \\cdot x \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} S\n     \\]\n\n6. Adding \\( S_{\\triangle BMO} \\) and \\( S_{\\triangle BNO} \\):\n   \\[\n   S_{\\triangle BMN} = \\frac{1}{m+1} \\cdot x \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} S + \\frac{1}{n+1} \\cdot x \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} S\n   \\]\n\n7. Equate the expressions for \\( S_{\\triangle BMN} \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{m+1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{n+1} \\cdot S = \\left( \\frac{1}{m+1} \\cdot x + \\frac{1}{n+1} \\cdot x \\right) \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} S\n   \\]\n\n8. Simplify to find \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{m+1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{n+1} = \\left( \\frac{1}{m+1} + \\frac{1}{n+1} \\right) \\cdot \\frac{x}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{(m+1)(n+1)} = \\left( \\frac{1}{m+1} + \\frac{1}{n+1} \\right) \\cdot \\frac{x}{2}\n   \\]\n\n9. Solve for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{(m+1)(n+1)} = \\left( \\frac{n+1 + m+1}{(m+1)(n+1)} \\right) \\cdot \\frac{x}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{(m+1)(n+1)} = \\frac{(m+n+2)}{(m+1)(n+1)} \\cdot \\frac{x}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1 = (m+n+2) \\cdot \\frac{x}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\