\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3)x^2 - (8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1)(2x) = 0\n\\]\n\nFactoring out \\(2x\\) from the equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n2x \\left[(2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3)x - (8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1)\\right] = 0\n\\]\n\nThis gives two solutions: \\(x = 0\\) (which corresponds to the point \\((0, 0)\\)) and:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1}{2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3}\n\\]\n\nThe length of the chord intercepted on the line \\(y = 2x\\) is the distance between the points \\((0, 0)\\) and \\(\\left(\\frac{8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1}{2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3}, 2 \\cdot \\frac{8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1}{2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3}\\right)\\). This distance is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1}{2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3}\\right)^2 + \\left(2 \\cdot \\frac{8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1}{2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{5} \\left| \\frac{8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1}{2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3} \\right|\n\\]\n\nTo maximize this length, we need to maximize the absolute value of the expression \\(\\frac{8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1}{2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3}\\). By analyzing the range of this expression using trigonometric identities and solving the resulting quadratic inequality, we find that the maximum value of the absolute value of the expression is 8. \n\nThus, the maximum length of the chord is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{5} \\times 8 = 8\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. Given the parametric form of the curve:\n   \\[\n   2(2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\theta + 3)x^2 - (8 \\sin \\theta + \\cos \\theta + 1)y = 0,\n   \\]\n   and we need to find the maximum chord length intercepted by this curve on the line \\( y = 2x \\).\n\n2. Substitute \\( y = 2x \\) in the equation of the curve:\n   \\[\n   2(2 \\sin \\theta - \\cos \\th